# PERF-GATHER-B1 row staging — 2026-06-10 (issue #41 chunk B1)
#
# Change: GatherRowStaging in gather_channel_samples — on the default
# (no-dedup) path each gathered sample writes into flat column-major row
# scratch (plain indexed stores), flushed once per row as per-column
# extend_from_slice memcpys. Replaces ~(2*num_pred + total_props) ≈ 45-60
# Vec::push calls (each with capacity check + len update) per sample —
# the store path that step-0 annotate showed as 22% of gather's cycles.
# Dedup-backend paths (opt-in) keep per-sample pushes (inline probe needs
# last-row interaction). Byte-identical: same values, same append order.
#
# Gates: bytes identical 5/5 cells (sha256 every iter); hash-locks 36/36
# default + parallel-tree-learning; lib 1487/1487 (incl. dedup units);
# lossless/modular/tree/dedup it 81/81; clippy clean.
#
# A/B (8 iters/side, loadavg 3.3 start — moderate; base = chunk-A build):
#   medians: terminal -0.72%  imac_dark +1.02%  noaa -1.81%
#            mobile -2.32%    clic097 -1.79%
#   MINS (load-robust): ALL 5 ours-min <= base-min —
#            terminal -0.9%  imac_dark -0.5%  noaa -2.0%
#            mobile -1.5%    clic097 -0.1%
# Read: consistent modest win on gather-heavy doc/screen cells
# (-0.5..-2.0% on mins); imac_dark's +1.02% median is tail noise (its
# min is FASTER). Quiet-box confirmation queued before headline numbers.
# Binaries: base /tmp/chunka_ours (= main e86a3e48+), ours this commit.
# Host: lilith (7950X, WSL2), no target-cpu=native.
#
# ── ADDENDUM: quiet confirmation (10 iters/side, calm start; a burst
#    arrived mid-run, loadavg 5.0 at end) ─────────────────────────────────────
# medians: terminal -0.31%  imac_dark -1.24%  noaa -0.99%
#          mobile -1.28%    clic097 +0.50%
# mins:    terminal 0.713==0.713  imac_dark -2.3%  noaa -1.9%
#          mobile -1.0%           clic097 1.110~1.111
# VERDICT: CONFIRMED — modest consistent win on gather-heavy doc/screen
# cells (-1.0..-1.3% median, -1.0..-2.3% mins); neutral on the photo
# cell (gather is only ~7.5% of CPU there) and on terminal medians.
# Matches the moderate-load grid's direction; claim stands at ~-1% wall
# on screens/docs for the staging alone.
